-- title:
--   Branch ideals extend to the geometric special fibre at a crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and $K \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ the intermediate field obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M*p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $X$ for the two-chart model `TwoChartModel A K j` with structure morphism $f =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and $X_k$ the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, with projections $\mathrm{pr}_1 \colon X_k \to X$ and the base-change structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Let $c_1 \colon C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 \colon C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with $C_1, C_2$ integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions into $X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ (each a morphism whose composite with the structure morphism of $X_k$ is $c_1$, resp. $c_2$). Assume $i_1, i_2$ cover $X_k$ on points, that the scheme-theoretic intersection $Z = C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and that $\operatorname{Nat.card} Z = n$ with $0 < n$. Let $\nu \in Z$, put $y = i_1(\mathrm{pr}_1^Z \nu) \in X_k$ and $x = \mathrm{pr}_1(y) \in X$, and assume: the images in $X$ of the generic points of $C_1$ and of $C_2$ both specialise to $x$ ($h_1$, $h_2$); the images in $X_k$ of these generic points both specialise to $y$ ($hk_1$, $hk_2$); and $i_2(\mathrm{pr}_2^Z \nu) = y$. Here, for a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow z$ in a scheme, the branch ideal is the preimage in the stalk at $z$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi$ under the specialisation map, i.e. the prime of the local ring cut out by $\xi$. The conclusion is the conjunction: the ideal generated by the image of the branch ideal of $h_1$ under the stalk map of $\mathrm{pr}_1$ at $y$, $\mathcal{O}_{X,x} \to \mathcal{O}_{X_k,y}$, equals the branch ideal of $hk_1$, and likewise the extension of the branch ideal of $h_2$ equals the branch ideal of $hk_2$.
--
--   This is the extension half of the comparison of branch ideals on the arithmetic surface $X$ and on its geometric special fibre $X_k$ at a crossing point of the two components $C_1, C_2$: the primes of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ attached to the two branches generate, after base change to $k$ and passage to the fibre, exactly the corresponding primes of $\mathcal{O}_{X_k,y}$. It feeds the local analysis of the crossings of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$, and is used in the invertibility and factorisation statement for the contracted kernels at such a point.
